I have finally ascended for the first time.

My last significant game ended with touching cockatrice corpse on dlvl
51 (read: VS level).

After about 10 bad starts I got a game going. Two things happened
early that made the game success. I found gauntlets of power (that
makes game much easier with weak Arc) and also found and managed to
identify a wand of polymorph. I polymorphed my kitten into purple
worm. Quite soon it ate some wraiths and suddenly it was XL 26, HP
200+ killing machine. I did Sokoban (got amulet of reflection) and
then Gnomish Mines without any major trouble.

Then I explored deeper. At dlvl 10 I found my only coaligned altar in
the game and established my stash there. During my return to Minetown
I eradicated all the soldiers and shopkeepers save Itzchak (my pet
purple worm Bianca eats them for breakfast by now). Then I explored
deeper. My game unfortunately had no portal to Fort Ludios and also no
Big Room (actually I have never seen BR so far). There was
uncomfortably close encounter with an air elemental at Rogue level. At
one moment I entered the niche marked with "ad aerarium" and was
teleported to dlvl 1 (if I were more careful I could notice the
direfent kind of teleport trap...). I thought that my pet is lost, so
I took and diversion to Mine Town to buy some more protection. When I
got down to my pet I found it is, quite unbelievably, still tame. It
was a bit of wait before I got up to XL 14; the Quest was no trouble.
My quest nemesis was promptly swallowed by Bianca before taking single
hit. My game contained lot of runing down and up again to my stash. At
the start of Medusa I ran into trouble with wand of create monster
toting gian or troll, but luckily ring of conflict took care of that.
There were no more trouble on Medusa (wand of cold and mirror). Then
Castle was again no big trouble. The wand of wishing had one or two
wishes in it I think.

Then I returned to my stash and started preparing for going down to
Gehennom. I wished for Grayswandir and spellbook of identify. I had
tons of rings to identify, but there was nothing extremely useful.
Especially no ring of slow digestion or teleport control (not to speak
of levitation). What was rather important was that I identified cursed
-4 boots of levitation for crossing the trap doors in Castle. I got
green dragon scale mail from some random killed dragon. Not enough
scrolls of enchant armor though, so I couldn't get too high AC (which
meant minotaurs had to be faced with caution). There was significant
trouble I faced at this moment: So far there were no magic markers.
Not in shops, not in Gnomish Mines, not anywhere. I tried to polypile
unicorn horns, but this was the moment I did a big mistake: I did not
realize that I have the chest with my complete stash in "line of fire"
and polymorphed the said chest. The stash was lost and all I got from
it was stack of boomerangs (which I did not use in the end). In the
destroyed stash was also my highly prized spellbook of identify.

With my stash gone, there was no reason to remain and I embarked to
the conquest of the Hell. At the Castle I left my pet upstairs in hope
of getting some wraith corpses in the Valley of the Dead. No luck this
time, but what I found there was brand new spellbook of identify.
Cool. I proceeded down to Gehennom. During the course of exploration I
got ring of slow digestion and ring of levitation. Unfortunately, no
ring of teleport control. With kerio's advice I refrained from slaying
Asmodeus. After long, painstaking mapping of Gehennom I arrived at
dlvl 51. There I had my final enchantment session. I wished for a
magic marker, because I found none. In the whole game I saw exactly
zero random generated magic markers. With the scrolls of enchant armor
I created GDSM and, by pure luck and stupidity enchanted it to +6! I
also did another major mistake in forfeiting a wish -- my wand of
wishing was 'a' in my inventory and somehow I managed to zap it and
then dismiss the wishing prompt with [enter]. I got completely useless
long sword. Somewhere I also got ring of teleport control, so I could
teleport upstairs to buy last bits of protection. I alchemized my
potions of healing, but unfortunately, bad luck again, I destroyed
good stack of them. I still had some, so it was not lost case. What
troubled me was only one scroll of gold detection. Never mind, I
teleported back to dlvl -50 to start the end game.

Killing Rodney wasn't hard, I had three wands of death at this time.
After invocation, I went down with my pet. I had still fresh memory of
jumping spell, so Moloch's Sanctum wasn't all that difficult (and
Bianca was rather efficient). Found the door to the temple with a
wand, entered and had another uncomfortable excursion into yellow
numbers. With HP at approximately 160 it was not nice. But I made it
and used cursed potion of GL to get out (with my pet, fortunately).

I started to go upstairs. Mysterious force was a bitch, really
annoying. Also annoying was waiting for Bianca to digest it's prey
before going upstairs. Rodney was visiting me often -- I had to kill
him 9 times (at first with wand of death, then I simply started to
melee him). After getting out of Gehennom, I it was rather quick to
get up and enter the Planes (the only incident was getting partial
amnesia after running into mind flayer). I was bit helpless on the
Plane of Earth, but with help form people on #nethack, I was quickly
up to the speed. I used my Orb of Detection to find portal on PoE. The
Plane of Air wasn't very hard thanks to conflict. Unfortunately, as I
entered the portal, Bianca was eating (I forgot to check). So on the
Plane of Fire I was alone. I used my only scroll of gold detection to
find the portal. On the Plane of Water I read my only (blessed) scroll
of genocide to eradicate all sea monsters. Then I just went to the
right and found portal just with searching for it. On the Astral Plane
I got very lucky. I appeared on the left side so I went to the left
altar, using mainly wand of teleportation and jumping (from spell) to
proceed (wearing ring of conflict). I killed Pestilence with wand of
death. Just few turns later, I was on the altar.

